From: OpenWrt FRITZ!Repeater 2400 port
Subject: wifi: ath9k: apply the QCA956x SoC quirks to QCN550x too

ath9k_of_init() picks the SoC specific setup by device ID.  QCN550x, added
by 005-wifi-ath9k-add-QCN550x-device-IDs.patch, appears in none of the
branches, so a node using compatible = "qca,qcn5502-wifi" silently loses
both get_mac_revision and is_clk_25mhz: is_clk_25mhz stays false, which
selects the wrong initval tables (ar9003_hw.c) and is evaluated again in
ar9003_phy.c and ar9003_eeprom.c.

QCN550x is a QCA956x derivative and uses the same bootstrap register
(QCA956X_RESET_REG_BOOTSTRAP, bit 2 = REF_CLK_40), so fold it into that
branch.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/init.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/init.c
@@ -744,7 +744,8 @@
 		u32 t = ath79_reset_rr(QCA955X_RESET_REG_BOOTSTRAP);
 		ah->is_clk_25mhz = !(t & QCA955X_BOOTSTRAP_REF_CLK_40);
 		ah->external_reset = qca955x_wmac_reset;
-	} else if (ah->hw_version.devid == AR9300_DEVID_QCA956X) {
+	} else if (ah->hw_version.devid == AR9300_DEVID_QCA956X ||
+		   ah->hw_version.devid == AR9300_DEVID_QCN550X) {
 		ah->get_mac_revision = ath79_get_soc_revision;
 		u32 t = ath79_reset_rr(QCA956X_RESET_REG_BOOTSTRAP);
 		ah->is_clk_25mhz = !(t & QCA956X_BOOTSTRAP_REF_CLK_40);
